---
description: Multiplayer must keep working; server stays authoritative
alwaysApply: true
---

- Never break: room create/join/rejoin, 4-character codes, host migration/start, nicknames,
  answers, secret mutiny, private item state, special allocation/lock, reveal or disconnect.
  Two browsers/laptops must complete the active block/event loop.
- The server (`server/src/engine.ts`) is the single source of truth: it owns
  phases, timers, allocations, scores and the correct answer. Clients render
  state and send intents; they never compute outcomes locally.
- The socket contract lives in `shared/src/types/index.ts`
  (`ClientEvents` / `ServerEvents`). Any protocol change
  updates that file first and both sides together.
- Validate all client input server-side (`allocationsValid`, phase checks,
  lock checks). Exact loot splits stay private until reveal; only totals,
  lock status and confidence flags are public.
- Client effects tolerate out-of-order/late state: cancel running timelines on phase/question
  changes and rehydrate from Zustand/socket state after reconnect.
- After protocol/flow changes, run the available root multiplayer smoke/e2e path with dev
  servers up. If no script covers the changed path, add coverage rather than invoking the
  archived experiment's smoke test.
